      "title": "典例精析与知识关系",
      "subtitle": "来源追溯与结果解释",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "number": "1",
          "text": "题目",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "A manufacturer obtains 70% of its components from supplier A and 30% from B. Their defect rates are 2% and 5%, respectively. A component is selected at random. Find (a) P(D), (b) P(B|D), and (c) P(B|D^c), where D denotes a defect. Interpret the results.",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 5
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "number": "2",
          "text": "完整英文解答",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "The supplier events A and B are mutually exclusive and exhaustive, so they form a partition of the sample space.",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "(a) By the law of total probability, add the joint probabilities for the two suppliers:",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "P(D) = 0.70 × 0.02 + 0.30 × 0.05 = 0.029",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "Thus, 2.9% of all components are defective. The rates are weighted by the supply proportions; an unweighted average would ignore the composition of the mixture.",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "(b) Given that the component is defective, Bayes' theorem gives:",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "P(B | D) = (0.30 × 0.05) / 0.029 = 15/29 ≈ 0.5172",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "B supplies approximately 51.72% of defective components, although it supplies only 30% of all components. Its higher defect rate increases its share within the defective group.",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "(c) P(D^c) = 1 − 0.029 = 0.971, while P(B∩D^c) = 0.30 × 0.95 = 0.285. Conditional probability therefore gives:",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "P(B | D^c) = 0.285 / 0.971 = 285/971 ≈ 0.2935",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "About 29.35% of non-defective components come from B. This is below its supply share because non-defective status is less likely under B than under A.",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "number": "3",
          "text": "方法归纳",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "本题两个后验概率分别以D和D^c为条件，分母随之变化。P(B|D)与P(B|D^c)不构成互补事件的概率；真正的互补关系为P(B|D)+P(A|D)=1。检查互补时，目标可以互补，条件必须相同。",
          "estimated_grid_lines": 3,
          "highlights": [
